    "updated_at": "2026-09-13T10:59:05Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the report and sorry for the delay, this landed in #545 and available in `0.14.0`.\n\n`calf-io` now has `suspend fun KmpFile.source(): kotlinx.io.RawSource`\n\nOpening is blocking on Android/iOS/Desktop, so call it from `Dispatchers.IO`.\n\nI went with kotlinx-io instead of a separate okio module: calf-io already depends on it. For your zip case the official bridge does the conversion:\n\n```kotlin\nimplementation(\"org.jetbrains.kotlinx:kotlinx-io-okio:0.9.1\")\n\nimport com.mohamedrejeb.calf.io.source\nimport kotlinx.io.okio.asOkioSource\n\nval zip = ZipInputStream(file.source().asOkioSource().buffer())\n```\n\nThis also removes the need for the canImportFile platform check, the same code now works everywhere.\n\nOn isFile: I left it as \"not a directory\". On Android every picked item is a content URI, so returning false would just make it always false there. The actual problem was that getPath() is not something you can open on Android, and source() is the answer to that. If you still need a \"is this a real file system path\" check after trying source(), let me know and we can add one.\n\nDocs: https://mohamedrejeb.github.io/Calf/filepicker/#streaming-with-kotlinx-io",
